.Dd November 24, 2026
.Dt MYC 1
.Os Spore
.Sh NAME
.Nm myc
.Nd inspect and control Mycelium units
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Ar command
.Op Ar unit
.Nm
.Cm logs
.Op Fl f
.Op Ar unit
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
sends service management commands to Mycelium on its control socket.
Use
.Cm list-units
to list loaded services, targets and timers.
.Cm status
shows the manager state or the status of a named unit.
.Cm cat
prints a unit's configuration.
.Pp
.Cm logs
shows the latest 50 system log lines.
Give a unit name to read its log, or use
.Fl f
to follow new lines.
For log queries a bare name such as
.Ar network
selects
.Pa network.service .
.Pp
Use
.Cm start , stop , restart
or
.Cm reload
with a full unit name to control it.
These operations require root.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
myc list-units
myc logs network
myc logs -f trustd.service
sudo myc restart network.service
.Ed
.Sh FILES
.Pa /etc/mycelium ,
.Pa /run/mycelium.sock ,
.Pa /var/log/syslog
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr mycelium 8
